# What research/i-have-adhd imports, and the exact state each dependency was read at.
#
# run.py loads two harnesses as modules (never copied): the upstream's own evaluation harness,
# vendored under vendor/i-have-adhd/ (its PIN there carries commit and sha256 per file), and the
# catalog's process layer research/lean-code/run.py. The contract is not enforced by this file — it
# is enforced by `run.py --selftest`, group `contract`, which gates `--matrix`: no paid cell runs
# while an imported symbol is missing or has changed the behaviour the group checks.
#
# KNOWN LIMIT: the contract test checks the symbols this harness relies on and the behaviours
# it exercises. An edit that keeps every signature and every checked behaviour but changes
# something else would not be caught.

